        <briefdescription>
<para>Generic mutator to remove const qualification from any type. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the input object.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>t</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The object from which to remove const qualification. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A non-const reference to the input object.</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-test-plus-utility-functions_1ga00ea8f3dfb7cb0ef39919065321cf62f" kindref="member">mut</ref></computeroutput> function template provides a safe and generic mechanism to remove the <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> qualifier from any type. It returns a non-const reference to the input object, enabling modification of objects that were originally declared as <computeroutput>const</computeroutput>. This utility is particularly useful in testing scenarios where controlled mutation of test data is required. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
